  "name": "ALLERGY SCREENING TRYPTASE",
  "code": "2657",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p>1. Tryptase is the most abundant protein in mast cells. During IgE mediated allergic reactions mast cells are activated and&nbsp;release inflammatory mediators including tryptase.<br>2. ImmunoCAP Tryptase measures the total tryptase levels including all forms of &amp;alpha;-tryptase and &szlig;-tryptase.<br>3.The baseline level of tryptase in the circulation reflects the number of mast cells.Elevated basal levels of serum tryptase and/or an underlying mastocytosis may be risk factors particularly in patients with history of severe reactions.<br>4. In anaphylaxis the triggering agent should be identified.Allergens commonly implicated in anaphylaxis are insect venoms,drugs, latex and foods.<br>5. Specific IgE antibody testing aids in the diagnosis of the triggering cause of anaphylaxis.</p>",
